{"id": "EUVD-2026-82178", "enisaUuid": "37c4b256-bc48-3e35-8deb-dd9ee5c0b80c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Fix DM I2C teardown race\n\nDM I2C adapters can remain visible to userspace while DM teardown is\nalready in progress. A concurrent i2c-dev transfer may then enter\namdgpu_dm_i2c_xfer() after the backing DM state has been torn down,\nleading to a NULL pointer dereference.\n\nCreate a devres group around the DM I2C adapter lifetime and release it\nat the start of dm_hw_fini(), before HPD, IRQ, and DM state are torn\ndown. This removes the I2C adapters first and waits for in-flight users\nto drain before the structures used by amdgpu_dm_i2c_xfer() disappear.\n\nThis fixes a teardown ordering race seen during device removal:\n\nBUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference\nRIP: amdgpu_dm_i2c_xfer+0x122/0x1c0 [amdgpu]\nCall Trace:\n__i2c_transfer\ni2c_transfer\ni2cdev_ioctl_rdwr", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ee385305e8902fa6fbfd66b5a112238292567b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6970ec944567f109ac4240f9aea58158ee8a18cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4ae30a12aa95942814957d8bc1ce7366a7107d7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93068", "GHSA-qm88-w7fg-5vv2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2bc61345-277d-3066-9de5-e400d3e3990a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "3f2cd0a8-7898-309e-add2-3156ffef9323", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5b3eca05cfb02ed0dbd7097c056fb08ce5f76fe3 <8ee385305e8902fa6fbfd66b5a112238292567b6"}, {"id": "671746f4-9f26-326c-9f9b-cb38d66c487a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5b3eca05cfb02ed0dbd7097c056fb08ce5f76fe3 <e4ae30a12aa95942814957d8bc1ce7366a7107d7"}, {"id": "84600c8c-5394-3aa3-ab9b-0621e2c0c22a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a470871b-bd0b-3fe2-8553-b7cba39a7ab6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "de8b35e6-0068-38be-b8c8-c6fe16ecba60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "e1f49982-e5aa-3067-a6df-b7ce82f3805b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "fbc55fe4-ca48-33b6-b2e2-ea534fa6579b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5b3eca05cfb02ed0dbd7097c056fb08ce5f76fe3 <6970ec944567f109ac4240f9aea58158ee8a18cd"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0597217c-02f5-3657-8f7f-e8b94bbae104", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}